    "title": "The €700,000 wealth tax line",
    "source_article": "late-tax-penalties.txt",
    "source_slug": "wealth_tax_en",
    "post_text": "Most owners will never meet Spain's wealth tax. If your Spanish assets are drifting toward 700,000 euros, you're not most owners, so you should know exactly where the line sits.\n\nThe tax applies to residents and non-residents alike, measured on total assets. Below 700,000 euros, nothing is owed. Above it, the tax bites incrementally, only on the value over the line, at progressive rates from 0.2 to 2.5 percent. No sale, no income, no trigger. Owning is enough.\n\nWhere you own matters as much as what you own, though, because the tax is shaped by local government. Madrid applies a 100 percent discount, so identical assets there mean a zero bill. Residents who live in their Spanish home also get an extra 300,000 euro allowance on that main home.\n\nWho actually gets caught? Two profiles. Non-residents holding one high-value property, and owners whose several Spanish assets, the apartment, the garage, the plot, quietly add up past the threshold without anyone doing the sum.\n\nThat second group is the one that worries me, because nobody sends a warning when you cross the line. The threshold doesn't announce itself.\n\nThe discipline costs one hour a year. Total your Spanish assets, and if you're anywhere near the line, get advice for your specific region, because in this tax geography changes everything.\n\nGeneral information, not tax advice.\n\n#SpanishTax #WealthTax #SpainProperty",
