    "title": "Your NRA number needs renewing yearly",
    "source_article": "nra-deadline.txt, rental-rule-changes.txt",
    "post_text": "1 February to 2 March 2026. If you rented out your Spanish property in 2025, write that window down, because your NRA registration number isn't a one-time formality. It renews annually.\n\nThe NRA, Numero de Registro de Alquiler, came into force on 1 July 2025. Every short, mid-term and tourist rental needs one, displayed on the listing, or you can't legally advertise on the big platforms.\n\nWhat surprises owners is that the renewal is a report, due even if you rented the place out once all year. You confirm the property is still used for rentals, declare any ownership changes, describe the year's rental activity, the different lets and their lengths, give the reasons for each stay, holiday, work or studying, and confirm that safety and habitability standards are maintained.\n\nYou file through the Land Registry your property is registered under, and if you already hold an NRA, expect a reminder email in January.\n\nTwo practical warnings before you go. The registry websites can be temperamental, and in Valencia the forms famously only download on a Microsoft computer, so some owners end up going in person. And your community can close the door entirely, because if the building has voted to ban tourist rentals, no registration code will be issued.\n\nThe habit that makes all of this painless? Keep a running log of every rental, dates, length and reason for stay, as the year goes. February you will thank August you.\n\nGeneral information, not legal advice.\n\n#HolidayRental #SpainProperty #SpanishHomeOwners",
